In Ricart-Agrawala, a node must receive replies from all others before entering the critical section, and nodes in the critical section shouldn't grant new replies. The invariant needs to ensure that if a node holds the lock, no other node can have received a reply from it during the current request cycle. The precondition `~replied(requester, responder)` prevents duplicate replies, but doesn't enforce that a node holding the lock hasn't already granted replies to multiple requesters in earlier cycles.

