Looking at the counterexample more carefully, it shows a state before node 0 enters where holds(1) is already true and replied(0,1) is true. This suggests node 1 entered first, then node 0 somehow got a reply from node 1 even though node 1 holds the lock. The safety violation occurs when both holds(0) and holds(1) become true simultaneously.

